      "side": 1,
      "message": "* **Suspicious Return Value in `test_enroll_start_failure`:**\nIn `test_enroll_start_failure`, you mock `focal_algo_enroll_start` to return `-1` (simulating a failure). However, the assertion expects the wrapper function to return `0`:\n```c\nint res \u003d fingerprint_enroll_start(fixture-\u003ealg);\nzassert_equal(res, 0, \"Expected 0 when focal_algo_enroll_start fails.\");\n\n```\n\n\nTypically, Zephyr subsystem drivers bubble up negative POSIX error codes (e.g., `-EINVAL`, `-EIO`) upon failure—which is correctly expected in `test_init_algo_init_failure`. If `fingerprint_enroll_start` truly returns `0` upon an underlying algorithm failure, it is likely swallowing the error, which points to a bug in `ft98xx_bio_alg.c`. If `0` is genuinely the intended behavior by design, please add a comment explaining why this API deviates from standard error handling.",
